WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.007
This tool gets you the data
for your assignment.

2
00:00:03.047 --> 00:00:06.914
It is not a replacement for
understanding how the numbers are made,

3
00:00:06.964 --> 00:00:09.010
so it has built-in learning checks.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.567
On Start here, enter your Northeastern email,

5
00:00:12.617 --> 00:00:15.701
then choose your group and the ranking period.

6
00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:18.771
Population and foreign born percent are given.

7
00:00:18.811 --> 00:00:23.110
You pick three more indicators; the
boxes start blank on purpose.

8
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:29.069
The Top 50 tab lists the fifty cities
where your group is largest.

9
00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:32.101
Its size in each city is your weight.

10
00:00:32.141 --> 00:00:34.560
The Data tab holds every city.

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.510
Income can be shown in 2024 dollars.

12
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.193
Results on the Weighted averages tab stay
hidden until you pass three checks.

13
00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:46.864
Step A: predict whether the
weighted average is higher,

14
00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:49.993
lower, or about the same as the plain average.

15
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:50.860
Then see why.

16
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:56.343
Step B: watch the short video, then
answer five questions,

17
00:00:56.393 --> 00:00:59.802
about your own data and about the ideas.

18
00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:02.260
Miss one, and you get a hint.

19
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.323
Miss the same question twice, and the
questions close for sixty minutes.

20
00:01:07.363 --> 00:01:10.958
Rewatch the video or practice, and
you get a new question.

21
00:01:10.998 --> 00:01:16.160
A third lockout means a meeting with your
instructor, who gives you a release word.

22
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.093
Step C: three values from your
top fifty are hidden.

23
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:23.542
Look each one up at the public
source and type it in.

24
00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:26.860
Three wrong entries mean
another sixty minute wait.

25
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.200
Then your results appear:

26
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.927
the weights, the weighted
average, the plain average

27
00:01:32.977 --> 00:01:38.222
and the national value, and how much of
your group lives in these cities.

28
00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:42.160
A completion code records your
wrong tries, to hand in.

29
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.508
Part 3 opens later, for the same cities:

30
00:01:45.548 --> 00:01:50.263
three crime rates per hundred thousand
residents, pooled over years.

31
00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:52.571
A city with no value is left out.

32
00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:54.110
The same checks apply.

33
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.720
Don't rush. Work in several
sittings, in the same browser.

34
00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.400
And tell us how it went:

35
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.010
your ideas are welcome.
